    "body": "Fixes #8134.\n\n`b'abc'.decode()` crashed the compiler: the constant decode in `_handle_simple_method_bytes_decode()` passed `encoding=None` on to `bytes.decode()` when the call had no arguments. It now falls back to `'utf-8'`, the default of `bytes.decode()`.\n\nTests: `tests/run/bytesmethods.pyx` gains the literal cases (no argument, encoding, encoding + errors) and one where the constant decode fails and the error must stay a runtime `UnicodeDecodeError`. Without the fix the file does not compile; with it `run.bytesmethods` passes (C backend, CPython 3.11, macOS arm64). No other bytes/str/unicode run test changes its result.\n\nAI assistance was used for finding the bug and for drafting the fix and the test.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-11-19T10:46:10Z",
